@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

rectangle "CameraX" as Camera
rectangle "Frame Scheduler" as Scheduler
rectangle "MediaPipe Pose" as Pose
rectangle "Coordinate Normalizer" as Normalize
rectangle "Landmark Smoother" as Smooth
rectangle "Tracking Quality Gate" as Gate
rectangle "Exercise Analyzer" as Analyzer
rectangle "Biomechanics Metrics" as Metrics
rectangle "Deterministic Rules" as Rules
rectangle "Cue Arbitrator" as Cue
rectangle "Overlay / TTS" as Output
queue "Telemetry Ring Buffer\nbounded / best-effort" as TelemetryQ
queue "Priority Persistence Queue\nbounded / reserved capacity" as PriorityQ
rectangle "Batch Writer" as Writer
database "Room / SQLite" as Room

Camera --> Scheduler : frame + monotonic timestamp
Scheduler --> Pose : newest eligible frame only
Pose --> Normalize : landmarks + visibility/presence
Normalize --> Smooth : canonical L/R + coordinate space
Smooth --> Gate : MovementFrame
Gate --> Analyzer : valid tracking only
Gate --> Output : setup/tracking guidance
Analyzer --> Metrics : phase + temporal state
Metrics --> Rules : metrics + confidence
Rules --> Cue : set-scoped FormEvent + FormEvidence[]\noptional repId
Cue --> Output : selected actionable cue

Analyzer --> TelemetryQ : raw telemetry / transient debug data
Analyzer --> PriorityQ : completed rep summary / CompactRepTrace
Metrics --> PriorityQ : final rep metrics
Rules --> PriorityQ : FormEvent + structured evidence
Cue --> PriorityQ : CueDelivery only when delivered
PriorityQ --> Writer : persist first
TelemetryQ --> Writer : best-effort batches
Writer --> Room : transactions

note bottom of Scheduler
Use newest eligible frames; never let a camera backlog grow.
end note

note bottom of Gate
Reject analysis for missing required landmarks, low confidence,
unsuitable camera view, or temporal discontinuity.
end note

note bottom of Cue
A detected FormEvent may be suppressed from feedback.
Only actual visual/TTS feedback creates CueDelivery.
TTS is offline-voice-only.
end note

note bottom of PriorityQ
PriorityPersistenceQueue is an in-memory scheduling lane.
It is not durable by itself; Room commit creates durability.
Keep it bounded with reserved capacity and drain before telemetry.
end note

@enduml
